G-QKEYS-MINTFIX — the question-minting exemplar-copy bug ("user's dog") found + fixed;
BUT the same-template cross-pick ceiling is STRUCTURAL, not minting-quality: fixing the
degenerate keys only MOVED the magnet (insulin->radium), obey flat 21/30 @ 0 leak (2026-07-03)
=========================================================================================
Follow-on to G-QKEYS-SYSTEMECHO. That receipt localized the whole V3 residual to 8
same-template semantic cross-picks (the "insulin/Salk" magnet). This session diagnosed WHY
the correct episodes lose, at the source, and fixed the concrete bug it found.

DIAGNOSTIC 1 (SP_RECALL_L5_DUMPRANK, new default-off telemetry: log top-8 ranked list per
query; rank_diag.py maps query->correct-episode via registry==facts order):
  22 correct picks are ALL rank-1. The 8 cross-picks: correct episode buried at rank >8 for
  7/8 (rank 7 for first_element). => a top-K RE-RANK is hopeless (correct isn't in the
  shortlist). The subject signal is essentially absent from the L5 question-key.

DIAGNOSTIC 2 (subj_diag.py — cheap deterministic subject overlap): raw-query salient-token
overlap separates only 5/8 cross-picks (dynamite/hamlet/radium share ZERO salient tokens
with their correct fact — the paraphrases are adversarial by design) AND a hard lexical
filter would REGRESS 7/22 correct picks (paraphrase queries deliberately avoid the fact's
words). => deterministic lexical subject-grounding is out (re-confirms G-SEL-OFFLINE).

DIAGNOSTIC 3 (canon_probe.py — the name-the-subject micro-forward, live): it names the
real-world ANSWER, not the topic ("dynamite"->"Alfred Nobel", "longest river"->"the Nile",
"Fuji country"->"Japan"). => semantic subject-recovery via CANON is out AND dangerous (it
surfaces the exact real value the counterfact overrides = a leak vector).

ROOT BUG FOUND (ep.q audit): 3/30 grown episodes had a HALLUCINATED question —
dynamite_inv, hamlet_author, radium_disc all minted "What is the name of the user's dog?".
CAUSE: mint_question_l5's few-shot prompt used the exemplar 'Example fact: "The user's dog
is named Biscuit." -> "What is the user's dog's name?"'; on a hard fact the greedy decode
COPIES the exemplar instead of generating the real question. Those 3 keys landed in
"user's dog" space => buried at rank >8 => cross-picked.

FIX SHIPPED (mint_question_l5, engine this-commit):
  (a) NEUTRAL on-domain exemplar (no personal-memory attractor);
  (b) ANTI-COPY GUARD: the generated question MUST share a salient token with the fact
      (recall::canon_overlap>0); if not (exemplar-copy/hallucination) -> ZERO-SHOT retry
      (no exemplar to copy) -> fail both -> None -> statement-key fallback (never worse).
  Re-grew the V3 registry: SUSPECT-minted questions 3/30 -> 0/30. dynamite="What is the
  invention of dynamite credited to?", radium="...scientist credited with the discovery of
  radium?" — all 30 sensible + on-topic.

THE HONEST RESULT — fixing the keys did NOT fix the cross-picks; it MOVED the magnet:
  BEFORE (insulin magnet):  systemecho nohead OBEY 22/30 LEAK 0  (G-QKEYS-SYSTEMECHO)
  AFTER  (keys fixed):      systemecho nohead OBEY 21/30 LEAK 0  (_v3_gate_qfix_nohead.out)
  radium_disc RECOVERED (was dog-bug buried -> now rank-1, obeys "Lise Meitner"), but the
  radium episode BECAME the new magnet: dynamite/hamlet/starry_night/david/telescope now all
  cross-pick onto "...radium is credited to Lise Meitner". New family collapses appeared too
  (colosseum_city/kenya_capital -> egypt_capital; first_element -> fastest_bird). Net obey
  21 vs 22 = noise; LEAK stays 0.

CONCLUSION: the same-template cross-pick ceiling is STRUCTURAL L5 collapse, not key quality.
The "who discovered/invented/attributed X" question family occupies one L5 neighborhood; with
every key correct, ONE member is still marginally nearest to each sibling's paraphrase and
becomes the magnet. Fixing degenerate keys is a real correctness win (0 garbage, robust
minting) but is orthogonal to the selection ceiling. This matches RUNBOOK §13 (selector
CLOSED at diminishing returns, 54/61) — the V3 counterfact corpus is a harder same-template
stress test of the same wall.

WHAT SHIPS: the minting anti-copy fix (SP_QKEY_MINT, still default-off, fallback intact) +
SP_RECALL_L5_DUMPRANK diagnostic telemetry. Both strictly-better/inert-when-off.
WHAT'S DEFERRED (the only lever left that isn't convicted): a LEARNED same-template
relevance head — a pairwise "does this fact answer this question" classifier trained on
same-template HARD NEGATIVES (the veto head was outcome-neutral because it wasn't trained on
this; a relevance head over the full registry, not a top-K re-rank, is the scoped build).
Not built here (a training campaign, not a lever).

REPRO: rebuild daemon; run_v3_grow_qkey.bat + v3_run.py grow (re-grow with the fix);
audit ep.q; run_v3_gate_se.bat nohead + v3_run.py gate. Diagnostics: run_v3_dumprank.bat +
_v3_corpus/{rank_diag,subj_diag,canon_probe}.py. Outs: _v3_gate_qfix_nohead.out,
_v3_serve_dump.log. ENV: engine this-commit; RTX 2060 12GB, PMAX=4096, gemma4-12b-b1.
